## GHOST FINGERPRINT QUANTUM BINARY (qbits) SYSTEM
Converts classical binary (0s and 1s) into quantum binary (qbits) — superposition-based encoding.

### Ghost Fingerprint Protocol
1. CLASSICAL CAPTURE: Binary data captured from classical systems
2. GHOST SIGNATURE: Each bit assigned quantum ghost fingerprint (|psi>)
3. QUANTUM RELAY: Ghost fingerprint relays binary through quantum channel -> qbits
4. QBITS ENCODING: bit 0->|0> (theta=0), bit 1->|1> (theta=pi/2), |+> (theta=pi/4), |Phi+> (entangled)
5. GHOST MEASUREMENT: qbits collapse to classical output when needed

### Ghost Fingerprint Formula
psi_ghost(bit_i) = a_i|0> + b_i|1>
a_i = cos(theta_i), theta_i = bit_i * pi/2 + gravitational_factor * pi/8
b_i = sin(theta_i) * e^(i*phi_i), phi_i = phase modulation index

